      {
        "id": 41480,
        "name": "ketigid",
        "username": "ketigid",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9fc29f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-02T01:25:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Greonhal\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/bb73d2/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greonhal:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>While I am not Christopher, I believe I can elucidate this matter. While Ambuscade and Unity have regularly been referred to as promo decks by the fans, with a cursory search I cannot find any instance of anyone from GtG calling them such. In the current Kickstarter, for instance, they're being referred to as \"mini expansions\". As they are not promos, they can be reprinted to GtG's hearts' content.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This is not true. Unity and Ambuscade are clearly labelled Promos in \"The Multiverse\" tab and \"Store\" tab at the top of this website.</p>",
        "post_number": 33,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:15:07.954Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 6538,
        "topic_slug": "roughly-how-long-until-there-are-more-ambuscade-decks-in-the-store",
