      {
        "id": 41481,
        "name": "drstein",
        "username": "drstein",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/cab0a1/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-02T11:05:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Paul\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/48/5862_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Paul:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Greonhal is correct. While the promo character cards are limited-run, the mini-expansions are not. While they are given away free as stretch rewards to our Kickstarter backers, they are fairly major game content that we don't want to limit only to people who know about / back us when we run a Kickstarter campaign.Also, as I mentioned in yesterday afternoon's Kickstarter update, we are likely to reprint an \"unlimitied edition\" run of all of the promo cards in several years so that people who want access to those characters can get them. The cards will have the same powers / game effect as the original promo cards, but will be visually distinct. The main reason that we are waiting is that we want to get all of the promo cards that we ever make into that pack, so we have to wait until Sentinels of the Multiverse is complete as a game, which won't be for a couple of years. The secondary reason though is that it rewards our early-adopter fans by giving them some minor game content that others won't have access to for a couple of years.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Hei Paul, in&nbsp; update # 17 of the Infernal Relics' Kickstarter you said:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Unity and Ambuscade will only be available through Kickstarter (and separately through our website once it ends if any remain) - they will not be part of any other expansion.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Unlike Unity, Ambuscade is completely free for <em>all</em> backers if we reach $75K!\"&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>So as far as I see it, it should be given the same treatment as other rewards, right? Well, my hope is that you do the opposite: if you reprint ambuscade, please reprint the other kickstarter-limted cards as well <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>By the way, as for the unlimited run: how about making the same card with a different image? It is definitely easy to identify them, and it will also provide a little something for those that have the old promo version <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
        "post_number": 34,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:15:08.027Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
